// Episode 2 level 2. Coordinates in metres, x = east, y = north, z = up.
// Setting: the Beacon 12 broadcast centre (a fictional local channel, "Beacon 12 - The City's
// Light"), taken over by the hive's servants to jam the emergency broadcast.
// Route: the street plaza (start on the road at the west end, facing east; the outside-broadcast
// van, the fountain, planters, the station's video billboard on the facade; the shotgun in the
// newsstand recess in the south wall) → the front doors → the lobby (reception desk, sofa,
// payphone and vending on the west wall) → the guard office through the south door (CCTV wall;
// the chaingun and the Blue security keycard) → the blue door in the lobby's north wall → the
// newsroom (cubicle crosses, the assignment desk, a news ticker and a monitor wall; three edit
// bays along the north wall) → the "on air" door east into Studio A (camera pedestals, the
// news set on its riser with the anchor desk, video walls north and east) → the dolly track
// across the studio fires channel 1: the floor rumbles and a scripted blast in the scene dock
// blows the studio's back wall open → the scene dock (stacked containers, scenery flats; pipe
// bombs) → the loading door south → Studio B, the "Jackpot Jamboree" game-show set (bleachers
// in the west, the stage with three contestant podiums in the east, the prize board on the
// south wall, an arcade corner in the south-west): climbing onto the stage fires channel 2
// (the two isolation booths in the south wall open, awake) and the Red studio key waits by the
// podiums → the green room door in the west wall → the green room (jukebox, pool table,
// vanity mirror, couch): its switch (channel 5) opens the door back into the lobby, the
// shortcut → the red door in the lobby's south wall → master control (two console rows, the
// monitor wall) → the door east to the tower foot → the tower, its floors side by side and
// each one lift higher: lift 1 (z 0 → 6) to the equipment floor (racks) → lift 2 (→ 12) to the
// transmitter hall: the cable gantry across the cable well fires channel 4 (a quake, and the
// gantry collapses 2 m for good) → out of the well up its stairs → lift 3 (→ 18) to the
// engineering floor → the chief engineer's office (the jetpack, the Yellow roof key) → the
// yellow door → the roof lift (→ 24) → the roof (open sky: an air handler, the satellite dish on
// its pad, the transmitter mast); stepping off the lift fires channel 6 (the maintenance shed
// in the east parapet opens, awake) → the uplink hut at the foot of the mast: the exit switch
// on its north wall puts the emergency broadcast back on the air.
// Secrets: (1) a crouch vent low in edit bay 3's east wall (vent 0.25-1.4 m) into the tape
// vault (rocket launcher, rockets, armour); (2) a crack wall in Studio B's east wall behind the
// game-show set (a barrel beside it, in the backstage lane): a stash with an atom and rockets
// (validate's "cannot be reached from the start" warnings for its items are a crack-wall stash,
// by design); (3) the maintenance platform on the transmitter mast at z 30, jetpack only (atom,
// armour; validate warns those "cannot be reached from the start", by design).
(
    name: "Dead Air",
    defaults: (floor_z: 0.0, ceil_z: 4.0, floor: "tile", ceil: "ceiling_tile", wall: "concrete"),
    music: Some("dead_air"),
    player_start: (pos: (3.0, 15.0), angle_deg: 0.0),
    sectors: [
